{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791070321,"nonce":"r2q7IRNLBNkaJ/jz1eDFIkzLmhM=","title":"CSS font-family passed only its first name, so the theme's monospace drew in the system sans","message":"Properties' font-family handler wrote the first family of the stack. The theme's mono stack starts with ui-monospace, which Blinc's registry does not know, so load_with_fallback_styled fell back to the system face: every code, kbd and pre drew in sans. Reproducer: tools/snapshot/scenes/Controls.hx before the fix, 'code' in sans.\n\nFix: the whole stack goes to the binding, which resolves it as a browser does (blinc_abi text.rs resolve_family): the first installed family (FontRegistry::has_font), else the first generic keyword as Blinc's generic face. ui-monospace, ui-serif and ui-sans-serif fall through to the families after them, since Blinc's generic monospace on macOS is Courier while a browser takes ui-monospace to be SF Mono or Menlo; they are used only when nothing after them is installed.","files":null}]}